<article class="env-lemma" id="0G9C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G9C">Lemma <span data-tag="0G9C">15.86.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $K \in D(R)$ with $H^ i(K) = 0$ for $i \not\in \{ -1, 0\} $. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$H^{-1}(K) = 0$ and $H^0(K)$ is a projective module and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^1_ R(K, M) = 0$ for every $R$-module $M$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> If $R$ is Noetherian and $H^ i(K)$ is a finite $R$-module for $i = -1, 0$, then these are also equivalent to </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="(3)"><p>
$\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^1_ R(K, M) = 0$ for every finite $R$-module $M$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The equivalence of (1) and (2) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0A5P" data-tag="0A5P">15.70.2</a>. If $R$ is Noetherian and $H^ i(K)$ is a finite $R$-module for $i = -1, 0$, then $K$ is pseudo-coherent, see Lemma <a href="/tag/066E" data-tag="066E">15.66.17</a>. Thus the equivalence of (1) and (3) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0G9A" data-tag="0G9A">15.79.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>